From 097e1a3c5bc56741925b7658f6008a082b186928 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 07:23:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/24] Compile graphics pipelines off the device and engine
 locks

A cold vkCreateGraphicsPipelines ran inside the draw that first needed
the pipeline: on the drain thread, with the device lock held for the
whole tranche and the engine lock for the whole draw. On a macOS 27.2
boot one draw held both for 8.6 s compiling the 368 062-word glass
fragment shader (pl_compile_us=8598624, pipe 46). A vCPU in the
IOSurface MMIO path holds the BQL and then waits for the device lock, so
QEMU's main loop, IRQs and the action BH stopped for those seconds and
the guest panicked on its own IPI timeouts.

Vulkan engine:
- The pipeline lookup moves ahead of the slot claim, the depth
  acquisition and anything recorded. A pipeline already in the map is
  used as before. Anything else is handed to a new compiler thread
  (pipeline_compiler) and the draw answers DrawAnswer::PipelinePending
  having changed nothing; a second ask for a key being compiled joins
  its ticket. Under the lock the draw only keys the pipeline (shader
  digests, memoized per allocation), makes the device checks and builds
  the layout and a compatibility-only render pass.
- The compiler thread holds no lock. It declares capabilities, runs
  spirv-val, builds both shader modules (kept per device by digest),
  calls vkCreateGraphicsPipelines and persists the pipeline cache. No
  creation of any kind is tried under the lock, including a cache-only
  FAIL_ON_PIPELINE_COMPILE_REQUIRED attempt: that flag does not promise
  the call will not block on the cache's internal lock.
- Results are published under the engine lock at the next draw or
  ticket query. Each ticket gets one answer: Ready, Failed(refusal) or
  DeviceRebuilt. A resumed draw carries its ticket back in, and a
  Failed ticket is that draw's refusal even when the negative cache
  does not remember it (out of memory), so the waiting packet cannot
  compile the same pipeline again; later independent draws may.
- DeviceLife owns the VkDevice, instance, pipeline cache and loader.
  A device loss mid-compile answers the waiting tickets DeviceRebuilt at
  once; the cache's layouts and passes go to the life's late list, and
  everything is destroyed when the compile lets go of the device. A
  result compiled on a replaced device is destroyed, not published.
- Compute pipelines are still created on the drain thread; their compile
  time is counted (cp_compile_us).
- driver_breadcrumb and driver_watch get a lane per thread (drain,
  compiler), since the two can be inside the driver at once.

Runtime:
- finish_stream's draw list can stop at a draw whose pipeline is
  pending. The packet keeps its streams, the walked stream state, the
  draw index and the chain state as an ExecContinuation, and is deferred
  through the AIR-translation machinery: no head move, no stamp, every
  other FIFO and display transaction held behind it, retried by the
  4 ms poll. A retry whose ticket is unanswered returns at once; once
  answered, the packet continues at that draw and never reruns what
  already ran.
- A continuation is resumed only by its ring entry (channel, next head,
  completion stamp, payload). Anything else at the head is refused by
  name and consumed, never run from the start. FIFO redefine/free and
  device reset drop it with a fail line.

Census: draw_phase pl_pending; engine_delta pipeline_pending and
pipeline_flight_joins; new pipeline_compile line (jobs, compile_us,
compile_max_us, module_us, queue_wait_max_us, published_stale,
failures_delivered, cp_compile_us, cp_compile_max_us); new
exec_pipeline_wait line (deferrals, retries, resumes, deferral_us,
deferral_max_us, mismatches, dropped).

Tests (dgx, GB10, taskset 0-4,10-14, --test-threads=1): lib suite 2214
passed, 1 failed (model::regs cursor bound, fails at the base too: the
worktree has no vendor/qemu). New:
- a cold pipeline compiles off the engine lock and a second ask joins
  it (compile held 300 ms at a test gate: engine try_lock never failed,
  the cold ask took 16-20 us, the joined ask 12-15 us)
- a device rebuilt mid-compile answers the wait and keeps the device
  until the compile returns
- out-of-memory compile delivered to its draw once, only later draws
  retry; a refused compile is remembered
- drain: a waiting draw holds the draws after it, the packet's stamp
  and the sibling FIFO, and nothing reruns; OOM reaches the packet once;
  a mismatched continuation is refused, not replayed; reset drops it;
  a 300 ms compile never holds the device lock (drain hold max
  43-286 us, vCPU wait max 5-259 us over three runs)
- the two driver lanes keep separate breadcrumbs and watch slots
Keying a 368 062-word module the first time costs 2.7-3.0 ms under the
lock (measured once, then the test was removed); later asks hit the
memo.

Clippy on backend-vulkan,host-window --all-targets: no warning in the
lines this commit adds; the 82 that remain are in code it does not touch
(chunks_exact_to_as_chunks and deprecated fetch_update under the 1.99
toolchain), down from 84 at the first run of this change.
tests/vk_engine_parity.rs does not compile at the base (color_input);
its calls were moved to execute_draw_request_blocking anyway.

Not verified: no guest boot; the backend-metal clippy arm (the
aarch64-apple-darwin target is not installed on dgx).
tests/vk_engine_batch (real metal2vulkan shaders, now through
execute_draw_request_blocking): 14 passed with llvm-dis on PATH.

